Package: BrainNetTest
Type: Package
Title: Global and Edge-Wise Inference for Brain Network Populations
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Maximiliano", "Martino",
           email = "maxii.martino@gmail.com",
           role  = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2437-4387")),
    person("Daniel", "Fraiman",
           email = "dfraiman@udesa.edu.ar",
           role  = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0482-9137")))
Description: Finite-sample inference for clinical and neuroimaging studies
    that compare independent populations of aligned binary, undirected brain
    networks. A whole-graph label-randomization test uses the edge-separable
    L1 analysis-of-variance score of Fraiman and Fraiman (2018)
    <doi:10.1038/s41598-018-23152-5> and is targeted to marginal edge-frequency
    shifts. Separate edge-wise exact tests report effect sizes and
    multiplicity-controlled selections. Validated S3 input and result classes
    provide print, summary, plot, and data-frame methods, while optional
    prefix-sum ablation diagnostics are explicitly descriptive. The same data
    contract can be used for other aligned binary network populations.
